</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_section"><a href="#S5" title="In Encoder-Decoder or Decoder-Only? Revisiting Encoder-Decoder Large Language Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">5 </span>Pretraining Results</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_section">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1" title="In 5 Pretraining Results ‣ Encoder-Decoder or Decoder-Only? Revisiting Encoder-Decoder Large Language Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">RedLLM and DecLLM scale at similar rates when increasing the compute (training Flops) and model parameters.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S5.SS0.SSS0.Px2" title="In 5 Pretraining Results ‣ Encoder-Decoder or Decoder-Only? Revisiting Encoder-Decoder Large Language Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">RedLLM lags behind DecLLM for compute-optimal training.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S5.SS0.SSS0.Px3" title="In 5 Pretraining Results ‣ Encoder-Decoder or Decoder-Only? Revisiting Encoder-Decoder Large Language Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">RedLLM scales slightly for few-shot learning but is poor at zero-shot; both largely underperform DecLLM.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S5.SS0.SSS0.Px4" title="In 5 Pretraining Results ‣ Encoder-Decoder or Decoder-Only? Revisiting Encoder-Decoder Large Language Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">RedLLM shows comparable and even better length extrapolation capability than DecLLM along model scaling.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S5.SS0.SSS0.Px5" title="In 5 Pretraining Results ‣ Encoder-Decoder or Decoder-Only? Revisiting Encoder-Decoder Large Language Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">The decoder self- and cross-attention in RedLLM show intriguing patterns under long context.</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_section"><a href="#S6" title="In Encoder-Decoder or Decoder-Only? Revisiting Encoder-Decoder Large Language Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">6 </span>Finetuning Results</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_section">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1" title="In 6 Finetuning Results ‣ Encoder-Decoder or Decoder-Only? Revisiting Encoder-Decoder Large Language Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">RedLLM shows high adaptability: matching and even surpassing DecLLM across scales after finetuning.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2" title="In 6 Finetuning Results ‣ Encoder-Decoder or Decoder-Only? Revisiting Encoder-Decoder Large Language Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Bidirectional input attention improves DecLLM greatly but doesn’t change the quality-compute frontier.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3" title="In 6 Finetuning Results ‣ Encoder-Decoder or Decoder-Only? Revisiting Encoder-Decoder Large Language Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">RedLLM has clear advantage over DecLLM on training and inference efficiency.</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_section"><a href="#S7" title="In Encoder-Decoder or Decoder-Only? Revisiting Encoder-Decoder Large Language Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">7 </span>Conclusion and Future Work</span></a></li>
